+## Lazy Iteration Convention
+
+Enumeration-style APIs — functions that produce multiple independent
+result items where each item can be computed without computing the rest
+— return **single-pass lazy iterators**, not materialized lists. This
+keeps memory usage independent of the result count and lets callers
+stop early when they only need the first few results.
+
+```python
+from algorithms.backtracking import permute, subsets
+
+# Results are streamed one at a time:
+it = permute([1, 2, 3])
+print(next(it))        # [1, 2, 3]
+print(next(it))        # [2, 1, 3]
+
+# Materialize explicitly when a list is really needed:
+print(list(subsets([1, 2, 3])))
+# [[1, 2, 3], [1, 2], [1, 3], [1], [2, 3], [2], [3], []]
+```
+
+The convention applies across categories, for example:
+
+- **Backtracking**: `subsets`, `subsets_v2`, `subsets_unique`,
+  `combination_sum`, `generate_parenthesis_v1` / `_v2`,
+  `generate_abbreviations`, `add_operators`, `array_sum_combinations`,
+  `unique_array_sum_combinations`, `get_factors`,
+  `recursive_get_factors`, `find_words`, `letter_combinations`,
+  `permute`, `permute_recursive`, `permute_unique`,
+  `palindromic_substrings`
+- **Tree**: `inorder` / `preorder` / `postorder` (iterative and `_rec`
+  variants), `level_order`, `zigzag_level`, `binary_tree_paths`,
+  `path_sum` / `path_sum2` / `path_sum3`, `left_view`, `right_view`
+- **Array**: `missing_ranges`, `summarize_ranges`, `delete_nth`,
+  `delete_nth_naive`, `three_sum`, `limit`, `flatten`
+- **String**: `fizzbuzz`, `fizzbuzz_with_helper_func`, `word_squares`,
+  `match_symbol`, `match_symbol_1`
+- **Matrix**: `spiral_traversal`
+- **Heap / Queue**: `max_sliding_window` (both implementations)
+- **Graph**: `get_factors`, `get_factors_iterative1`,
+  `get_factors_iterative2`
+- **Math**: `gen_strobogrammatic`
+- **Bit Manipulation**: `subsets`
+- **Set**: `find_keyboard_row`
+
+APIs whose first result inherently requires the whole computation —
+sorting algorithms, `merge_intervals`, `top_1`, `group_anagrams`,
+`find_all_cliques`, `k_closest`, `top_view`, `bottom_view` — keep
+returning materialized containers.
+
+Backward compatibility notes:
+
+- Historical `*_iter` variants (`permute_iter`,
+  `palindromic_substrings_iter`, `flatten_iter`) remain available and
+  behave as aliases of their now-lazy counterparts.
+- The legacy two-argument accumulator forms still work:
+  `inorder_rec(root, acc)`, `preorder_rec(root, acc)`,
+  `postorder_rec(root, acc)` and `flatten(items, acc)` fill the
+  provided list and return it.
+- Argument validation that raised eagerly before (for example
+  `fizzbuzz(0)` raising `ValueError`, or `max_sliding_window` with a
+  non-positive window size) still raises at call time, before any
+  consumption.
+- Both `max_sliding_window` implementations share the same edge-case
+  semantics: a window larger than the input yields no results, a
+  window exactly the input size yields a single maximum, and a
+  non-positive window size raises `ValueError`.
+
