+"""Contract tests for the library-wide lazy iteration convention.
+
+Enumeration-style public APIs (functions that produce multiple independent
+result items, where the first item can be computed without computing all
+of them) return single-pass lazy iterators. This module pins down the
+contract:
+
+1. The return value is a single-pass iterator: ``iter(r) is r`` and it is
+   not a materialized container (list / tuple / set / dict).
+2. The yielded items match the historical content and order exactly.
+3. Results are produced lazily: the first item is available without
+   computing the whole result set.
+4. APIs whose first result inherently requires the whole computation
+   (sorting, global selection, grouping) keep returning materialized
+   containers.
+"""
+
